===== .claude/rules/forge-docker-compose.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Docker Compose. `compose.yaml` holds the shared setup; `compose.override.yaml` (loaded automatically) holds local changes.
`depends_on` uses the long form with a `condition` (the bare list form is rejected); `condition: service_healthy` needs a `healthcheck` on that service.
`develop.watch` syncs or rebuilds on file changes (`docker compose watch`); `profiles` keep optional services off by default.
Variables named like `*PASSWORD*`, `*SECRET*`, `*TOKEN*`, `*API_KEY*` under `environment` or build `args` hold a `${VAR}` reference or nothing (`*_FILE` is fine); a committed `.env` is rejected.
Published ports 5432, 3306, 6379, 27017, 9200, 5672, 11211 and 1433 (short syntax) bind to `127.0.0.1`: Docker-published ports bypass ufw and firewalld.
docker compose runs outside Claude Code's sandbox, so these checks are a real boundary.

===== .claude/rules/forge-docker.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Docker. Multi-stage builds keep build tools out of the final stage; the checks require the final stage to run as a non-root `USER`.
`RUN` installs from the lock file: `npm ci`, `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, `uv sync --locked`, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `yarn --immutable`; `bun add` and `uv add` are rejected. Cache mounts (`RUN --mount=type=cache,target=...`) speed them up.
`ARG` and `ENV` names like `*TOKEN*`, `*SECRET*`, `*PASSWORD*`, `*API_KEY*` are rejected (`*_FILE` is fine); build secrets use `RUN --mount=type=secret,id=...`.
Base images name a version tag or a digest (not `latest`); each Dockerfile has a `.dockerignore` that excludes `.env` files.
Claude Code's sandbox blocks docker unless the user lists it in `sandbox.excludedCommands`; docker commands then run outside the sandbox.

===== .claude/rules/forge-github-actions.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

GitHub Actions. Actions are pinned to a full commit SHA with the version in a comment (`uses: actions/checkout@<sha> # v5`); zizmor's unpinned-uses check rejects tags.
Workflows set `permissions: {}` at the top and grant each job only what it needs (excessive-permissions).
`actions/checkout` sets `persist-credentials: false` unless a later step pushes (artipacked).
Attacker-controllable `${{ }}` values (issue and PR titles, bodies, branch names) inside `run:` are rejected (template-injection): pass them through `env:` and use the shell variable.
`pull_request_target` and `workflow_run` run with secrets on untrusted code; zizmor's dangerous-triggers check rejects them.

===== .claude/rules/forge-python.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Python project managed with uv. Tools run from `.venv/bin`. Type checking: basedpyright.
Inside `async def`, the checks reject blocking calls that ruff's ASYNC210, ASYNC230 and ASYNC251 detect (sync HTTP clients, `open()`, `time.sleep`).
Ignore comments name their rule (`# pyright: ignore[ruleName]`), and a changed file may not gain suppression comments.
Before writing a utility, search the codebase for an existing helper (warn-once and logging helpers, `utils` functions) and reuse it instead of adding a near-duplicate.

